{"bug":"K001","report":"A","v":"missed","ref":"8. Tuple deserialization can consume a sibling’s value incorrectly","evidence":"“successful visitors are not checked for unconsumed elements” concerns surplus tuple elements. The report does not identify ignored unknown nested fields leaving contents unread and misaligning later derived-struct fields."}
{"bug":"K002","report":"B","v":"found","ref":"2. Tape container accessors truncate contents and panic on empty containers","evidence":"“Their slices omit one node because count excludes the header.” Names all four shortcut accessors, missing final elements, and empty-container panics, identifying the required off-by-one slice defect."}
{"bug":"K003","report":"D","v":"found","ref":"3. Long decimals produce different values depending on their input offset","evidence":"“The code saves the starting digit’s byte value where it needs a starting position, incorrectly bypassing the slow conversion path.” Identifies the byte-versus-offset error at correct.rs:168 and documents incorrect long-decimal values."}
{"bug":"K006","report":"B","v":"found","ref":"4. Extra tuple elements can become the following field’s value","evidence":"“Container visitors are not checked for complete consumption.” The example returns ((1,2),3) from [[1,2,3],4], explicitly showing unread inner-array elements shifting into a later tuple field."}
{"bug":"K006","report":"D","v":"found","ref":"4. Extra tuple elements are accepted and can replace sibling values","evidence":"“Validate container consumption after visitors return” and “the outer sibling comes from inside the inner array.” Identifies the missing consumption check and demonstrates surplus elements replacing a later tuple field."}
{"bug":"K008","report":"B","v":"partial","ref":"6. Empty sequences without length hints serialize as incomplete JSON","evidence":"“serialize_seq(None) followed by end()” returns “\"[\"”; “The first flag incorrectly doubles as an indication that the closing delimiter was already written.” Identifies the same closing-state defect, but only for unknown-length sequences, omitting the required known-length case."}
{"bug":"K008","report":"D","v":"partial","ref":"5. Unknown-length empty containers serialize as incomplete JSON","evidence":"“Serializing an empty filtered iterator through Serde’s collect_seq returns Ok(\"[\").” The report identifies confused empty/closed state, but limits the sequence finding to unknown lengths and does not identify empty known-length sequences."}
